	"prompts": {
		"resourceSelection": "{{workOrderSection}}\n\n{{assetSection}}\n\nTASK: Select the best {{resourceName}} for the label \"{{label}}\" from the available options.\n\nThe label \"{{label}}\" indicates what type of {{resourceName}} is needed for this specific work order and asset combination.\n\nSELECTION CRITERIA:\n- The label \"{{label}}\" indicates what type of {{resourceType}} is needed\n- Consider how the {{resourceType}} relates to the work order and asset context\n- Look for the most relevant {{resourceType}} for this specific work order on this asset\n\nAVAILABLE {{resourceNameUpper}}:\n{{optionsText}}\n\nYou MUST respond with ONLY the external ID of the best matching {{resourceName}}. Do not include any explanation or additional text.\nIf none of the available {{resourceName}}s are good matches, respond with an empty response.",
		"templateSelection": "WORK ORDER CONTEXT:\n- Name: {{workOrderName}}\n- Type: {{workOrderType}}\n- Description: {{workOrderDescription}}\n\nASSET CONTEXT:\n- Name: {{assetName}}\n- Type: {{assetType}}\n- Description: {{assetDescription}}\n\nAVAILABLE RESOURCES:\n{{resourcesSection}}\n\nAVAILABLE TEMPLATE CANVASES:{{canvasSection}}\n\nTASK: Select the best template canvas for this work order, or decline if none fit. Consider:\n1. How well the canvas name matches the work order type/purpose\n2. Whether the available resources can fulfill the template's requirements\n3. The overall fit between the work order context and the template's expected resources\n\nIf none of the templates are a good fit for this work order, respond with NONE. A generic all-resources layout will be used instead.\n\nRespond with ONLY the canvas ID (external_id) of your selection, or NONE, nothing else."
	},
